.TH PDRIVE-APP 1 "November 2026" "PDrive for Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdrive-app \- desktop application of PDrive for Linux (tray icon, status window)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdrive-app
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.br
.B pdrive-app \-\-remove\-integrations
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdrive-app
is the desktop application of PDrive for Linux, an unofficial Proton Drive
client. It runs and supervises
.BR pdrived (1)
(restarting it with an increasing delay if it fails), shows an icon in the
notification area (StatusNotifierItem) and a status window with the account,
used space, recent activity and settings, and lets you sign in and out.
When the session is no longer accepted (expired or revoked), the daemon is not
restarted: the status window opens and the browser sign-in starts again.
.PP
Only one instance runs: starting the application again shows the status window.
Closing the window does not quit the application; use
.B Quit
in the tray menu, or send
.BR SIGTERM .
The daemon is then stopped cleanly and the drive unmounted.
.PP
On GNOME, the tray icon needs the
.I AppIndicator and KStatusNotifierItem Support
extension. PDrive for Linux is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, Proton AG.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without opening the status window. Used by the autostart entry, which
the settings window creates in
.IR ~/.config/autostart .
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-integrations
Remove the entries added to the file managers (see
.BR "FILE MANAGERS" )
and exit. The uninstall script runs it.
.SH FILE MANAGERS
At every start, when the setting
.B file_manager_integration
is on (the default; the settings window has a switch), the application adds the
drive to the file managers that are installed, whatever the current desktop
session is. Nautilus needs nothing: its sidebar entry comes from the
CloudProviders interface.
.TP
.B Dolphin
An entry "Proton Drive" in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/user-places.xbel ,
only when that file already exists.
.TP
.B COSMIC Files
Only if
.I com.system76.CosmicFiles.desktop
is installed: a favorite in
.I ~/.config/cosmic/com.system76.CosmicFiles/v1/favorites
and two context-menu actions in
.I .../v1/context_actions
that run
.BR "pdrive keep\-offline" " and " "pdrive free\-up\-space"
(see
.BR pdrive (1)).
COSMIC Files cannot limit them to the drive, so they appear on every file and
do nothing, with a notification, outside it.
.PP
Only the entries recognised as ours are changed or removed; the rest of the
files is left as it is. Packages never touch these user files: run
.B pdrive\-app \-\-remove\-integrations
before removing the package to clean them up.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PDRIVE_VERBOSE
When set, the daemon logs HTTP requests and SDK debug messages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdrive/config.toml
Settings, edited by the settings window (see
.BR pdrived (1)).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/pdrive/pdrive.log
Log used when there is no systemd journal (default
.IR ~/.local/state/pdrive/pdrive.log ).
Otherwise, when not started from a terminal, the log of the application and of
the daemon goes to the journal:
.B journalctl \-\-user \-t pdrive
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdrive (1),
.BR pdrived (1)
.PP
https://github.com/bpresles/PDrive\-for\-Linux
